00:23:55,361 --> 00:24:00,360
Lucky Charms is like the one, the hot one that goes off. Everybody loves it.

300
00:24:00,361 --> 00:24:04,360
For the ladies, Smart Start, it seems like we're all trying to watch our weight.

301
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:12,660
In the mid-1800s, America was also watching its weight, struggling to shed the hefty breakfast foods of a different era.

302
00:24:13,360 --> 00:24:19,680
We moved away from being a farm country where people were working hard in the fields to more sedentary jobs.

303
00:24:19,681 --> 00:24:21,343
But people didn't change their diets.

304
00:24:21,344 --> 00:24:23,680
They were still eating those huge, heavy breakfasts.

305
00:24:24,520 --> 00:24:27,837
Something had to give, and what gave was their health.

306
00:24:27,838 --> 00:24:29,680
Gout was rampant in the 1800s.

307
00:24:29,681 --> 00:24:35,680
In 1863, Dr. James Caleb Jackson, a strict vegetarian,

308
00:24:36,380 --> 00:24:39,900
concluded that the fiberless American diet was responsible for the epidemic.

309
00:24:40,800 --> 00:24:42,260
He turned to nature for the remedy.

310
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:44,980
He developed granula with a U.

311
00:24:45,500 --> 00:24:51,840
It was basically a dried whole wheat that was rich in bran,

312
00:24:52,080 --> 00:24:56,900
and he dried it, toasted it, dried it again, and chopped it up.

313
00:24:56,901 --> 00:24:58,320
It was hard as a rock.

314
00:24:58,321 --> 00:25:03,420
You had to soak it in water overnight to be able to eat it, but it was healthy.

315
00:25:06,020 --> 00:25:08,866
Sanitarium owner Dr. John Kellogg took notice.

316
00:25:08,867 --> 00:25:12,640
Dedicated to healing through holistic medicine and nutrition,

317
00:25:13,540 --> 00:25:18,620
Kellogg recognized that Jackson's granula could help his patients, if only they could get it down.

318
00:25:18,621 --> 00:25:26,120
He worked out a technique by rolling the grain and then baking it to have it flake.

319
00:25:26,121 --> 00:25:32,124
And so he created the first flaked whole grain cereal, much lighter than the granola that Dr.

320
00:25:32,125 --> 00:25:33,480
Jackson came up with.

321
00:25:33,620 --> 00:25:35,480
Easier to chew, quicker to prepare.

322
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:39,920
With the improved flake, the Kellogg's Cereal Company opened its doors.

323
00:25:40,620 --> 00:25:42,280
Soon they introduced other grain flakes.

324
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:43,960
The public loved it.

325
00:25:45,180 --> 00:25:46,840
Dozens of cereal companies followed.

326
00:25:46,841 --> 00:25:54,160
At Nature's Path Cereal Company in Washington State, cereal is made around the clock using

327
00:25:54,161 --> 00:25:56,160
the latest technique called extrusion.

328
00:25:56,161 --> 00:26:01,360
This is the beginning of the process where raw materials come in, they get lifted up

329
00:26:01,361 --> 00:26:03,160
into this station.

330
00:26:03,161 --> 00:26:10,740
They go from here over into a conveyor system that takes it into a mixing tank, it'll send

