00:26:10,741 --> 00:26:14,120
it over to the extruder.

332
00:26:14,121 --> 00:26:18,720
At this point in the process, the vast majority of cereal companies use a different technique

333
00:26:18,721 --> 00:26:21,240
called batch processing.

334
00:26:21,241 --> 00:26:26,180
With it, grains and flavoring agents are placed in pressurized cylindrical drums.

335
00:26:26,181 --> 00:26:32,360
As the drums rotate, the ingredients are cooked at a low temperature for several hours.

336
00:26:32,361 --> 00:26:39,660
With extrusion, the raw grains and wet ingredients are quickly pressure cooked using high heat.

337
00:26:39,661 --> 00:26:44,220
Once the grains are in the system, flavoring agents are added, and the mixture is sent

338
00:26:44,221 --> 00:26:45,220
to the extruder.

339
00:26:45,221 --> 00:26:52,440
Here we are at our extruder where we take dry ingredients, we mix them with our wet ingredients

340
00:26:52,441 --> 00:26:54,700
like sugar, salt, water, and barley malt.

341
00:26:54,701 --> 00:26:56,840
They go through the extrusion process.

342
00:26:56,841 --> 00:27:02,880
Then they get over here, they go through this tube in a dough form, they go into the former

343
00:27:02,881 --> 00:27:06,620
where they get cut into little beads.

344
00:27:06,621 --> 00:27:10,620
From here on, the batch and extrusion methods are identical.

345
00:27:10,621 --> 00:27:15,320
To form the beads, the cereal dough is pushed through a small circular die and then into

346
00:27:15,321 --> 00:27:16,320
a slicer.

347
00:27:16,321 --> 00:27:25,380
The beads are then sent to the flaker room, where they're squashed between two steel drums

348
00:27:25,381 --> 00:27:31,240
and 40,000 pounds of pressure.

349
00:27:31,241 --> 00:27:35,740
Fully shaved, the flakes are vacuumed through pipes and into the cooking system.

350
00:27:35,741 --> 00:27:38,500
The flakes come from the bead room overhead.

351
00:27:39,020 --> 00:27:41,700
They get sent over into this shaker belt.

352
00:27:42,100 --> 00:27:45,420
It's shaking to equally distribute those flakes across this belt

353
00:27:45,421 --> 00:27:48,700
so they can be consistently heated through the ovens.

354
00:27:52,140 --> 00:27:55,980
Once inside the ovens, the flakes dance under a series of tubes.

355
00:27:56,180 --> 00:27:58,220
They cook them with streams of hot air.

356
00:27:58,580 --> 00:28:02,580
You can see the tubes in here that cause the agitation in the flakes.

357
00:28:02,581 --> 00:28:10,040
Those flakes come out of the oven and on this belt, they get transferred to a bucket elevator and into the cooling process.

358
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:17,160
The flakes move through an air cooler and in this case, into a blend of other cereal ingredients.

359
00:28:20,620 --> 00:28:27,280
The blended grains now enter the area where each cereal company distinguishes its products, the flavoring screw.

360
00:28:27,281 --> 00:28:33,280
Here we've taken our blended cereal where we've combined multiple products together.

361
00:28:33,281 --> 00:28:37,280
They come into this screw here where we add the coating.

362
00:28:37,281 --> 00:28:40,280
The coating is sprayed equally into this product.

363
00:28:40,281 --> 00:28:46,280
The coating gets sprayed through these nozzles and equally distributed on this product.

364
00:28:46,281 --> 00:28:51,280
This coating's got a little almond flavor with a little bit of sugar.

