00:29:54,781 --> 00:29:59,200
The product here will go along this belt into the packaging lines where it will ultimately

378
00:29:59,201 --> 00:30:03,600
be sent to the supermarket for consumption.

379
00:30:03,601 --> 00:30:08,640
After drifting from its intended direction, cereal has come full circle.

380
00:30:08,641 --> 00:30:14,300
At Nature's Path, whole grains and flavoring agents are all grown organically.

381
00:30:14,301 --> 00:30:17,720
Because of their success, other companies are following suit.

382
00:30:17,721 --> 00:30:22,720
The baby boomers were the ones who grew up on sugary cereals and other junk foods.

383
00:30:22,721 --> 00:30:28,300
And today, they're now in their 40s, 50s, 60s, and they want product that's good for

384
00:30:28,301 --> 00:30:29,300
them.

385
00:30:29,301 --> 00:30:36,600
In 2005, cereal sales in the U.S. topped $6 billion.

