The pancakes that pass enter a blast freezer.

456
00:35:12,580 --> 00:35:16,700
As you can see, now that the products come through the freezer in a frozen state,

457
00:35:16,701 --> 00:35:20,440
It goes up the conveyor, goes over into a scale system.

458
00:35:20,940 --> 00:35:24,840
The scale system looks for a certain combination of weight versus count.

459
00:35:25,420 --> 00:35:28,240
So we can get 48 McGriddles per bag.

460
00:35:28,720 --> 00:35:34,020
Once it finds that combination, it'll drop it into a bag, and then we bag it before we put it into a box.

461
00:35:37,040 --> 00:35:40,260
The pancakes are now ready to meet the other McGriddle ingredients.

462
00:35:40,261 --> 00:35:49,280
From separate facilities around the country, pre-cooked bacon and sausage, fresh eggs and cheese are shipped to individual McDonald's restaurants.

463
00:35:50,540 --> 00:35:56,380
There, eggs are cooked, ingredients are assembled, and the McGriddle sandwich is ready for pickup.

464
00:35:57,720 --> 00:36:02,500
What you'll get is 450 calories, 32% of which are from fat.

465
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:05,920
But you'll also receive 40% of your daily protein.

466
00:36:05,921 --> 00:36:12,360
For those on the run looking for something a little lighter, the Carnation company is

467
00:36:12,361 --> 00:36:15,200
stirring up an alternative.

468
00:36:15,201 --> 00:36:18,360
Breakfast in a glass.

469
00:36:18,361 --> 00:36:23,640
In the early 1960s, Carnation began to experiment with powdered products that would supply all

470
00:36:23,641 --> 00:36:26,440
of the nutrients in a typical breakfast.

471
00:36:26,441 --> 00:36:31,980
The magic combination turned out to be nonfat milk powder for protein, vitamins and minerals,

472
00:36:31,981 --> 00:36:35,840
maltodextrin, a natural cornstarch as a carbohydrate,

473
00:36:35,841 --> 00:36:39,320
calcium, thickener, and sugar and cocoa for taste.

474
00:36:41,160 --> 00:36:44,000
Instant Breakfast was ready for the public.

475
00:36:44,001 --> 00:36:46,480
The product manager on Instant Breakfast

476
00:36:46,481 --> 00:36:48,460
was my father, Jack McDonald.

477
00:36:48,461 --> 00:36:50,980
So he would bring home packets of the powder,

478
00:36:50,981 --> 00:36:52,540
and these were prototypes,

479
00:36:52,541 --> 00:36:55,200
and he would ask my brother and sister and I to try them.

480
00:36:55,201 --> 00:36:58,440
So it was many, many months of testing this product,

481
00:36:58,441 --> 00:36:59,740
and it had to taste good.

482
00:36:59,741 --> 00:37:01,840
And of course, as a child, I liked the chocolate.

483
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:06,780
Just mix one envelope carnation instant breakfast with fresh whole milk.

484
00:37:07,420 --> 00:37:08,120
Stir.

485
00:37:08,140 --> 00:37:11,560
In 1965, carnation instant breakfast was launched.

486
00:37:12,020 --> 00:37:14,120
Indirectly at the real head of the household.

487
00:37:14,380 --> 00:37:19,000
The marketing campaign focused on moms as the gatekeeper for their families.

488
00:37:19,001 --> 00:37:23,680
And I remember a woman that you would describe probably as a traditional housewife.

489
00:37:24,080 --> 00:37:25,020
Breakfast skippers.

490
00:37:25,540 --> 00:37:29,200
And she would say to the camera, don't be a breakfast skipper.

491
00:37:29,201 --> 00:37:31,520
make sure you have a nutritious breakfast.

492
00:37:31,860 --> 00:37:34,580
Don't be a breakfast giver. Try the balance breakfast.

493
00:37:34,581 --> 00:37:36,160
The concept caught on fast.

494
00:37:36,660 --> 00:37:40,260
An instant breakfast took its place next to other symbolic images of the era.

495
00:37:41,920 --> 00:37:43,480
Okay, let's start with strawberry.

496
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:48,480
Carnation food scientists are constantly trying to keep instant breakfast

497
00:37:48,481 --> 00:37:50,420
a step ahead of the latest food trends.

498
00:37:51,260 --> 00:37:53,260
And so far, they've been successful.

499
00:37:53,780 --> 00:37:55,760
Everybody, let's try the chocolate right now.

500
00:37:55,761 --> 00:38:04,040
The recent addition of a dark chocolate flavored mix provides the same amount of antioxidants as a cup of green tea.

501
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:08,840
Carnation also produces zero sugar products.

502
00:38:10,340 --> 00:38:15,320
Inside the original chocolate powder is a vitamin and mineral packed 130 calories.

503
00:38:16,640 --> 00:38:21,180
Just 1% of the daily value for fat and 9% of the protein allowance.

504
00:38:22,220 --> 00:38:24,000
Not bad for a breakfast made in a laboratory.

505
00:38:25,760 --> 00:38:32,400
Getting another of America's favorite breakfast foods to the table requires a slightly simpler procedure.

506
00:38:33,980 --> 00:38:41,300
In 2005, Americans consumed 580 million McMuffins and 237 million McGriddles.

507
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:47,080
Breakfast Tech will return on Modern Marvels here on the History Channel.

508
00:38:48,540 --> 00:38:52,220
We now return to Breakfast Tech on Modern Marvels.

509
00:38:55,760 --> 00:39:03,600
On land, or at sea, the classic American breakfast isn't complete without a side of toast.

510
00:39:05,020 --> 00:39:06,920
Making it is a simple process.

511
00:39:07,500 --> 00:39:12,700
Bread in, radiant heat scorches the bread, and out comes a crisp piece of toast, ready to eat.

512
00:39:14,300 --> 00:39:18,860
But originally, toasting bread had a more practical purpose, preservation.

513
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:21,920
It's got roots back in the Middle Ages.

514
00:39:21,921 --> 00:39:28,160
As soon as bread was invented, cooks pretty quickly realized that if you toast it, it lasts longer.

515
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:35,740
With electricity came the first toasters, odd-looking contraptions made of wire and heating coils.

516
00:39:37,020 --> 00:39:40,520
Thanks to some faulty designs, toasting bread was like playing with fire.

517
00:39:41,420 --> 00:39:48,000
One of the signs of the early toasters where you used to have to turn it around with some kind of device,

518
00:39:48,140 --> 00:39:50,740
usually your fingers, hoped you didn't get burned.

519
00:39:51,920 --> 00:39:55,760
There were other problems as well.

520
00:39:55,761 --> 00:40:01,160
The heating coils made from iron or copper would become brittle and break.

521
00:40:01,161 --> 00:40:07,040
In 1905, engineer Albert Marsh invented an alloy called nichrome, a mixture of nickel

522
00:40:07,041 --> 00:40:13,260
and chromium that could be heated thousands of times without breaking.

523
00:40:13,261 --> 00:40:17,340
Toasters were ready to burn their way through breakfast history.

524
00:40:17,341 --> 00:40:23,820
Tom Osden and his son, Stefan, have been collecting toasters since 1989.

525
00:40:23,821 --> 00:40:28,860
Lining the walls of their family home are hundreds of toasters, relics that exhibit

526
00:40:28,861 --> 00:40:32,660
the evolving inventiveness of American toaster manufacturers.

527
00:40:32,661 --> 00:40:35,900
They start rather simple.

528
00:40:35,901 --> 00:40:37,780
They become more elaborate.

529
00:40:37,781 --> 00:40:42,640
And then as the depression comes in, they're simplified.

530
00:40:42,641 --> 00:40:46,340
Then the World War II comes and there's a metal shortage.

531
00:40:46,341 --> 00:40:52,580
And so you're still having relatively simple things with little metal.

532
00:40:52,581 --> 00:40:57,960
Now in the 50s, it's the advent of the pop-up toaster.

533
00:40:57,961 --> 00:41:02,180
And now you're beginning to get something more complicated again.

534
00:41:02,181 --> 00:41:09,580
You find that some of the toasters in the 50s and 60s are made rather elaborate timing

535
00:41:09,581 --> 00:41:12,000
mechanisms.

536
00:41:12,001 --> 00:41:13,580
They pop out.

537
00:41:13,581 --> 00:41:19,020
Also you find that the toasters are getting much cheaper and frankly a lot of them from

538
00:41:19,021 --> 00:41:25,420
the 60s on are very cheaply made and probably no longer American.

539
00:41:25,421 --> 00:41:29,420
As they worked their way through history, several toasters stood out.

540
00:41:29,421 --> 00:41:35,760
In the 1920s, toasters capable of cooking a complete breakfast hit the market.

541
00:41:35,761 --> 00:41:41,400
One part here on top we have a waffle maker.

542
00:41:41,401 --> 00:41:45,080
The next one we have the actual toaster itself.

543
00:41:45,081 --> 00:41:46,680
Make your toast.

544
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:52,780
And next device here is for frying bacon.

545
00:41:53,460 --> 00:41:56,140
And finally, here we have an egg poacher.

546
00:41:56,760 --> 00:42:00,340
So you could use a whole breakfast at your table.

547
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:05,160
Some toasters went beyond cooking and into the mildly entertaining.

548
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:09,520
The famous 1930s toast-a-later came with a view to the action.

549
00:42:09,521 --> 00:42:14,520
It's got a little porthole in the middle and you can watch it go past.

550
00:42:14,521 --> 00:42:20,520
It is an amusing toaster because it goes in as a piece of white bread and falls out at the other end.

551
00:42:20,521 --> 00:42:25,520
It's a toast. Voila! A perfect piece of toast.

552
00:42:25,521 --> 00:42:30,520
Other toasters were pieces of movable art. Function was secondary.

553
00:42:30,521 --> 00:42:36,520
There's a beauty in them. And we get to some very wonderful shapes.

554
00:42:36,521 --> 00:42:42,000
We also get some toasters which are bizarre in us what they can do.

555
00:42:42,001 --> 00:42:45,900
It's complicated a matter which is very simple.

556
00:42:47,580 --> 00:42:50,760
Although at times simplicity has been lost in the design,

557
00:42:51,220 --> 00:42:53,960
it's the practical advances that have kept toasters viable,

558
00:42:54,440 --> 00:42:55,680
like the pop-up feature.

559
00:42:57,820 --> 00:42:59,800
With the original pop-up toasters,

560
00:43:00,260 --> 00:43:04,360
electricity from the outlet heats up a temperature sensor called a thermocouple.

561
00:43:05,320 --> 00:43:10,620
Once it hits a pre-calibrated temperature, it releases a catch, sending the toast carriage upward.

562
00:43:11,760 --> 00:43:14,420
The thermocouple simultaneously shuts off the electricity.

563
00:43:16,080 --> 00:43:20,740
Since the 1970s, manufacturers have returned to producing multitasker toasters.

564
00:43:21,800 --> 00:43:26,840
Toasters have morphed into bagel bakers, hot dog eaters, pizza parlors, and sandwich shops.

565
00:43:28,360 --> 00:43:34,040
I find from the sheer appearance, they are no longer very interesting.

566
00:43:34,360 --> 00:43:36,300
They do many more things.

567
00:43:36,800 --> 00:43:42,000
They produce good toast, but they're not very pretty or interesting.

568
00:43:42,880 --> 00:43:46,720
For collectors, the golden years of toaster design are over,

569
00:43:47,180 --> 00:43:49,140
and a new era of utility has begun.

570
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:55,020
But inventions like the toaster will continue to inspire new alternative breakfast foods.

571
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:58,680
As food science and technology continue to merge,

572
00:43:59,020 --> 00:44:01,760
who knows what the next generation will be eating for breakfast?

573
00:44:01,761 --> 00:44:07,760
One area where I think is a huge advance is handheld breakfast.

574
00:44:07,761 --> 00:44:10,760
I think the granola bar is sort of cereal in a bar.

575
00:44:10,761 --> 00:44:14,760
I could see a bacon and egg bar, maybe a pancake bar.

576
00:44:14,761 --> 00:44:16,760
Why not even pancake chips?

577
00:44:16,761 --> 00:44:22,760
Meanwhile, aboard the USS John C. Stennis, breakfast is finally over.

578
00:44:22,761 --> 00:44:27,760
As sailors clean up and prepare to go to work, all across America,

579
00:44:27,761 --> 00:44:37,260
All across America, the utensils of breakfast technology continue to squeeze, slice, bake, and mix the most important meal of the day.

580
00:44:40,860 --> 00:44:45,820
This man knew his invention could change the world, but he didn't do it for science or even the money.

581
00:44:46,020 --> 00:44:47,860
He did it for a reason few might suspect.

582
00:44:48,420 --> 00:44:54,440
Alexander Graham Bell's incredible machine was inspired by his work with people who couldn't even hear.

583
00:44:54,441 --> 00:45:00,500
Don't miss Alexander Graham Bell and the Astonishing Telephone on Man Moment Machine, next on the History Channel.

